# Git Commit Messages

Follow [Conventional Commits v1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

## Required format

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

`<filename>` - <what changed in this file>
`<filename>` - <what changed in this file>
```

## Subject

- **feat** — new feature (MINOR in SemVer)
- **fix** — bug fix (PATCH in SemVer)
- Other allowed types: build, chore, ci, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, revert
- Scope: optional logical area (header, movies, ui, apps, projects, router, api)
- Description: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period
- Breaking changes: `type(scope)!: description` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer

## Body (project convention)

- Blank line after subject
- One line per materially changed file
- Format: `` `<filename>` - short explanation ``
- Order by importance; skip lockfiles unless they are the main change

## Example

```
feat(header): update header links with current page

`HeaderLinks.tsx` - highlight active route and sync nav links with current page
`utils.ts` - add helper to resolve current page from pathname
```

Never commit `.env`, credentials, or secrets.
